# Business collateral that landed in the repo root: sales decks, pricing
# frameworks, financial scoping and invoices. These are commercial documents,
# not source, and some are internal — they should live in the drive, not in a
# code repository where every collaborator inherits them.
/*.pdf
/*.pptx
/*.docx
/*.png
/Genesis_X_*.html
/Nova_*.html

# Vendored upstream with its own git repository — not a submodule.
infra/mailcow-dockerized/

# Hyperswitch deployment config. These carry the live payment stack's
# admin_api_key, jwt_secret and card-vault master_key — they were committed,
# and the secret scan only passed because gitleaks-action is licence-gated
# into a no-op. The redacted *.example templates next to them stay in git so
# the deployment is still reproducible.
#
# The values remain in git history: rotating them and purging the history is
# still outstanding, and the secret-scan job stays red until it is done.
# Named individually rather than *.toml: superposition_seed.toml carries no
# credentials and stays in git.
infra/hyperswitch-config/router.toml
infra/hyperswitch-config/vault.toml
infra/hyperswitch-config/docker_compose.toml

# Playwright journey screenshots — run output, regenerated by the suite
tests/e2e/**/shots/
